+{
+  "file": "src/agents.ts",
+  "snippet": "  maxTurns: 5,",
+  "cause": "The multi-turn `triage` agent was defined without a `store`, so Genkit has no persisted snapshots to load and rejects any resume by sessionId, while the single-turn flows and the `refundAgent` (which has `store`) work.",
+  "evidence": "Before the fix, `triage.loadChat({ sessionId })` failed with \"FAILED_PRECONDITION: getSnapshotData requires a persistent store. Provide a 'store' when defining 'triage'.\"; `refundAgent.loadChat` got past that check and only reported \"Snapshot session ... not found\" for an unknown id. After adding `store` (the shared FileSessionStore), a two-turn test (\"My order is A-1001.\" then loadChat by the returned sessionId and \"What is its status?\") answered with A-1001's shipped status, ETA and tracking code."
+}
